                ],
                [
                    1181.0,
                    218.0
                ],
                [
                    33.0,
                    218.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "15-2 The Board agrees to provide funds for teachers who desire to attend instructional area conferences, with prior approval by the appropriate District administrator. In order to implement this provision, the District agrees for the 2003-2004 school year to provide $75,000. For the 2004-2005 school year, the District agrees to budget $124,334 plus a cost of living increase for the 2003-2004 school year. Both parties agree to review this article at the 2004 bargaining session as an item mutually brought to the table. This amount shall be increased each school year by an amount commensurate with the percentage increase to the base salary as specified in Article 44. Travel, meals, lodging, registration fees, and substitute teachers shall be deemed appropriate ex-penses to the Board, unless otherwise mutually agreed. Such teachers attending conferences and meetings shall be granted sufficient leave time to attend without loss of compensation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                32,
                242,
                1181,
                388
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    32.0,
                    242.0
                ],
                [
                    1181.0,
                    242.0
                ],
                [
                    1181.0,
                    388.0
                ],
                [
                    32.0,
                    388.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "15-2-1 A leave committee consisting of four (4) class-room teachers, appointed by the Association, and one (1) administrator, appointed by the Superintendent or his/her designee, will review all applications for leave and make appropriate recommendations.",
            "block_bbox": [
                33,
                412,
                1180,
                457
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
